---
title: Salmon Pasta Bake
description: Creamy pasta bake with leeks, canned salmon, and peas
image: https://www.everydayhealthyrecipes.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Creamy-Salmon-Pasta-.jpg
source: https://www.everydayhealthyrecipes.com/salmon-leek-pasta-bake-asparagus/#recipe
servings: 4
---

= Sauce =

In a large pan, melt @unsalted butter{1 1/2%tbsp}(21g), add @leeks{1%medium}(finely chopped), and cook gently until softened, about ~{5%minutes}. Do not let the leeks brown.

Add @all-purpose flour{2 1/2%tbsp}(20g). Stir until the flour is thoroughly combined.

Gradually pour in @milk{2 3/4%cups}(660ml), stirring until smooth. Add @vegetable bouillon{1 1/2} and @Dijon mustard{1 1/2%tsp}(7.5ml). Cook, stirring continuously, until the mixture starts bubbling.

Remove from heat and stir in @sour cream{3%tbsp}(40g)(or cream cheese or yogurt) and @white pepper{} to taste.

= Pasta & Breadcrumbs =

Meanwhile, cook @fusilli pasta{3%cups}(250g) in salted water until al dente.

In another pan, toast @panko breadcrumbs{1/2%cup}(50g) in @salted butter{1%tbsp}(14g) until golden brown. Set aside.

Preheat the oven to 220°C.

= Assembly & Baking =

In a casserole dish, combine the pasta with the sauce as well as @peas{1%cup}(frozen), @parsley{1/4%cup}(finely chopped), and @salmon{350%g}(canned and drained). Taste and adjust seasoning as needed.

Scatter the toasted panko breadcrumbs over top.

Bake in the preheated oven for ~{15%minutes}.